to the flight tracks that have been  created something is happening we don't  really know what it is but clearly the  Russians now are talking about  withdrawing uh civilians from Kirsten  which by which they mean the Russians  who want to go and those Russians who  may have collaborated with uh the  authorities and there are queues  building up for the ferries to get out  we don't know how big these cues may  become but clearly the Russians are  preparing to do one of two things in  Kirsten either to withdraw their troops  or to fight for it we don't know which  um the general sirotherkin he is  believed last September to have said to  Putin we need to withdraw we need to  draw a safer line a bit further east  than we are now or we'll be surrounded  Putin is believed to have said no you've  got to stay sarovicin seems to be  softening up with the Russian public  possibly for for as Dominic said either  a withdrawal or a really big battle  around cursing in which maybe new  weapons might be used we'll see  meanwhile the other front is still very  active up in the northeast of the  country of course the uh offensive that  the ukrainians launched at the end of  August goes on they've liberated kharkiv  and the battle now is all about cremina  the road north from criminas the p-66  very big Highway it runs from Criminal  North through satova and North to  droiska right on the border of Russia  that is the main Highway by which the  Russians supply all of their forces  further uh South uh in luhanskondon yet  they can supply them from Russia of  course but this is the main line and  there's a tremendous battle going on now  for the p-66 that Highway the ukrainians  have got it within artillery range  they're attacking parts of it the  Russians are digging in and hanging on  at svato and we'll see how they get on  but cremena is also being surrounded on  two sides at the moment by the  ukrainians there's quite a fierce battle  going on there and a little bit further  south the batmut the Russians are  pushing forward this is the Wagner group  versus the 93rd mechanized infantry of  the ukrainians they're making some  progress of bakmut but it's not going to  do them all that much good unless they  can push right further west than they  probably can't so there's some really  active fighting going on here of course  all our attention is in uh Kirsten  that's strategically more important but  an awful lot of people are fighting  ferociously at the moment for the p66 up  there north of cremina so this battle  this war is entering a new phase as we  get towards the winter the ukrainians  are making a big push to get their gains  nailed down before the weather closes in  and makes operations a bit more  difficult for them Jane back to you  Michael thanks very much well coming up  later here on Sky News Michael is going  to be asking your questions uh you've  just heard from him professor Michael  Clark and it's about the war in Ukraine  if you have any questions you would like  to uh answered seven o'clock this  evening he will be answering those you  can email news at sky.com or scan the QR  code on your screen right now and then  we can put them to him a little later on  tonight

